WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.9 · Marketing & Communications
Campaigns and calls to action

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your first campaign is often the launch itself: one result, one audience, one clear call to action.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.281
A campaign is a time-bound, coordinated push to get one result from one audience, with one clear call to action. For something new, the first campaign is often the launch itself.

4
00:00:26.681 --> 00:00:27.281
The campaign brief

5
00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:35.278
Goal and audience: One result you can measure, from one audience. For example: Twenty households pre-order bread from our bakery in March.

6
00:00:35.278 --> 00:00:45.126
Insight and message: What the audience cares about, and what you will say. For example: They want fresh bread nearby: “Fresh each morning, baked by local trainees.”

7
00:00:45.126 --> 00:00:52.752
Call to action: One specific, easy step: book, sign up, pre-order, join or apply. For example: Pre-order by message before Friday.

8
00:00:52.752 --> 00:01:03.800
Plan and risks: Channels, timeline, budget, owner, risks and approvals. For example: Four weeks of flyers and a chat group, led by the founder, small print budget.

9
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:04.800
Why it matters

10
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:10.104
1. A focused push gets results that scattered posts do not.

11
00:01:10.104 --> 00:01:15.407
2. Your launch is the first real test of your messages.

12
00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:21.341
3. A brief helps everyone involved pull in one direction.

13
00:01:21.741 --> 00:01:22.341
Where you will use it

14
00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:26.904
1. Your launch: first participants, customers, members or volunteers.

15
00:01:26.904 --> 00:01:31.467
2. Your measurement: the result compared with the goal.

16
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:37.030
3. Your next campaign, improved by what you learned.

17
00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.030
What to avoid

18
00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.222
Several calls to action in one campaign.

19
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:47.896
Advocacy claims without evidence, or ignoring the rules on political activity.

20
00:01:47.896 --> 00:01:54.570
No review afterwards of what to keep and what to change.

21
00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.970
You write a campaign brief for your launch.

22
00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.970
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:05.570
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
